From: Shelley Vohr <shelley.vohr@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:19:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix: don't apply a window's draggable regions under a child
 WebContentsView (#54936)

* fix: don't apply a window's draggable regions under a child WebContentsView

Every WebContentsView in a window was asked whether a point is in one of its
draggable regions, and any yes made the point part of the title bar. A view
stacked above another one's `app-region: drag` area therefore could not be
clicked there. Only the frontmost WebContentsView at the point is asked now.

* fix: skip subtrees that take no events and cover more stacking cases in specs

The walk now skips a child that cannot process events, like the views event
targeter does. New specs: a view that covers part of the window, a hidden
view, and a plain View over a draggable region.
